` declarations are not hoisted. Some older files in this project have the wrapper first (before the flow), which creates a runtime `ReferenceError`. Fix this ordering when refactoring.\\n- **Duplicate Export Prevention**: When applying a sequential two-step edit (first remove `export` from the flow, then add an async wrapper at the bottom), always verify with `expand_code_chunks` after the first step before applying the second — especially if the file was already partially modified by a previous session. Skipping this check leads to duplicate `export async function` declarations that cause TypeScript errors."}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: find_and_replace_code', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span'}
