## ✅ Writing Tools API Integration Tests — Complete

### Files Created

| File | Tests | What It Tests |
|------|-------|---------------|
| `flows/__tests__/paraphrase-text.test.ts` | 9 | Mode instructions (standard/formal/fluent/creative/simplify), empty input validation, dash-stripping, empty model output error |
| `flows/__tests__/grammar-checker.test.ts` | 9 | Corrected text, unchanged text passthrough, markdown preservation, `result.output` fallback, empty output error, whitespace trimming |
| `flows/__tests__/humanize-text.test.ts` | 9 | Humanized output, `result.output` fallback, empty/whitespace model errors, error wrapping, markdown preservation |
| `use-cases/__tests__/RunAiToolUseCase.test.ts` | 16 | Tool not found, guest allow/block, rate limiting, credit deduction, free-tier fallback, AI flow execution, credit refund on failure, generation logging, usage metadata |
| `api-client/__tests__/WritingToolsApiClient.test.ts` | 12 | Correct endpoint construction, `Result.ok` on success, `ApiError` passthrough, generic Error wrapping, unknown error wrapping, `writingToolApi` alias |
| `services/__tests__/WritingToolRegistry.test.ts` | 17 | `getTool` for all key tools, aliases, case-sensitivity, unknown tools, `getAllTools` completeness, ToolConfig structure validation |

### Key Technical Patterns Used

- **Module-load mock pattern**: `definePrompt` runs at module-load time, so `mockReturnValue` is set via a top-level `jest.fn()` before the import, not inside `beforeEach`
- **`delete (global as any).window`**: Required before importing server-only modules in jsdom test environment
- **Layered mocking**: `RunAiToolUseCase` tests mock Genkit, flows index, and WritingToolRegistry to prevent ESM parse errors from the `genkit`/`yaml` packages
- **`Result` pattern**: All assertions use `.isSuccess`, `.isFailure`, `.getValue()`, and `.error` correctly per the project's `Result<T, E>` class

