2026-04-02 23:03:52.559 | 43144 (43144) | DEBUG    | Processing tool event with attributes: {'gen_ai.tool.name': 'expand_code_chunks', 'gen_ai.tool.call.id': 'toolu_vrtx_01Nx99V3Eak9cFp4xiZECnfz', 'tool_arguments': '{"file_path": "AGENTS.md", "line_ranges": [[1,80]]}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: expand_code_chunks', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span', 'tool_response': 'Successfully expanded code chunks in AGENTS.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # AGENTS.md — Arkan Project Guide\n   1 \n   2 ## Subagents — Delegate Tasks to Specialists\n   3 \n   4 Rovo Dev has access to specialized subagents that should be used for relevant tasks. **Always delegate to a subagent when one matches the task** — they have deeper expertise, tighter focus, and produce better results than the general agent.\n   5 \n   6 Subagent definitions live in `.rovodev/subagents/`. Use the `invoke_subagents` tool to call them.\n   7 \n   8 ### Available Subagents & When to Use Them\n   9 \n  10 | Subagent | Use For in This Project |\n  11 |----------|------------------------|\n  12 | **Next.js 15 AI Development Assistant** | New pages/routes in `src/app/`, Server Components, data fetching, Next.js 15 App Router patterns, AI SDK integrations |\n  13 | **Next.js 15 Server Actions + Form Handling Master** | Forms with React Hook Form + Zod, Server Actions in `src/app/`, `useActionState`, progressive enhancement |\n  14 | **shadcn/ui Component Builder Assistant** | New components in `src/components/ui/`, extending Radix primitives, CVA variant systems, accessible UI patterns |\n  15 | **Animation + Motion Assistant** | Framer Motion animations, micro-interactions, Tailwind CSS animation utilities, reduced-motion support |\n  16 | **Data Table + Dashboard Master** | Admin dashboard tables (`src/components/admin/`), TanStack Table, Recharts charts, `src/app/admin/dashboard/` |\n  17 | **Next.js 15 Real-time & WebSocket Patterns Master** | SSE/WebSocket features, real-time notifications, live data feeds, `src/app/api/` streaming endpoints |\n  18 | **State Management with Redux Agent** | Complex Zustand store design (`useBuilderStore`, `useGenerationUIStore`), state architecture decisions |\n  19 | **Bug Hunter** | Investigating and reproducing bugs, writing detailed bug reports, analyzing error traces from `errors.txt` |\n  20 | **Code Review Checklist Agent** | Code quality reviews, security checks, consistency audits before merging |\n  21 | **AI Coding Best Practices Recommender Agent** | Refactoring guidance, design pattern improvements, general code quality analysis |\n  22 | **Async/Await Implementation Agent** | Refactoring async code in AI flows (`src/ai/flows/`), fixing unhandled promise patterns |\n  23 | **AI Software Scalability Advisor Agent** | RAG system scaling (`src/modules/rag/`), Qdrant performance, API route bottlenecks |\n  24 \n  25 ### Project-Specific Delegation Patterns\n  26 \n  27 - **Adding a new writing tool**: Use **Next.js 15 AI Development Assistant** for the page (`src/app/writing-tools/<tool>/page.tsx`) + **shadcn/ui Component Builder Assistant** for the UI component (`src/components/writing-tools/`) + **Next.js 15 Server Actions + Form Handling Master** for the form logic.\n  28 - **Adding a new Genkit AI flow**: Use **Next.js 15 AI Development Assistant** (understands Server Actions and `\'use server\'` patterns in `src/ai/flows/`).\n  29 - **Admin dashboard features**: Use **Data Table + Dashboard Master** for tables/charts in `src/app/admin/` and `src/components/admin/`.\n  30 - **Fixing a reported bug**: Use **Bug Hunter** to reproduce and document, then the relevant specialist subagent to fix.\n  31 - **New shadcn/ui component**: Use **shadcn/ui Component Builder Assistant** — always extend existing primitives from `src/components/ui/` rather than rebuilding.\n  32 - **Real-time notifications or live updates**: Use **Next.js 15 Real-time & WebSocket Patterns Master** for SSE endpoints and `EventSource` client hooks.\n  33 - **Code review before merging**: Use **Code Review Checklist Agent** to audit security, consistency, and TypeScript correctness.\n  34 \n  35 ### Example: Invoking a Subagent\n  36 \n  37 ```\n  38 Use the "shadcn/ui Component Builder Assistant" subagent to build a new\n  39 FileUploadCard component in src/components/ui/ that accepts a file via\n  40 drag-and-drop, shows upload progress, and follows the existing shadcn/ui\n  41 patterns in this project (cn() utility, CVA variants, forwardRef).\n  42 ```\n  43 \n  44 ---\n  45 \n  46 ## Project Overview\n  47 \n  48 - **Name:** Arkan — AI-powered academic and professional writing platform\n  49 - **Language:** TypeScript (strict mode, 100% type safety goal)\n  50 - **Framework:** Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Actions, PWA via `@ducanh2912/next-pwa`)\n  51 - **React version:** React 18 (with strict mode enabled)\n  52 - **AI backend:** Google Genkit 1.x with Ollama models (Gemma 2B, Phi-3 Mini, Llama 3.1)\n  53 - **Database/Auth:** SQLite (Drizzle ORM) for data and local auth; Firebase Admin SDK (server-side only) for legacy support and FCM.\n  54 - **File Storage:** Local filesystem-based storage (`storage/uploads/`).\n  55 - **Vector store:** Qdrant (for RAG) via `@qdrant/js-client-rest`.\n  56 - **No Client-side Firebase**: The project is fully independent of client-side Firebase SDKs. Authentication is local (SQLite + JWT), and files are served locally. Do not re-introduce `firebase/auth`, `firebase/app`, or `firebase/firestore` in client components.\n  57 - **UI library:** shadcn/ui (Radix UI primitives) + Tailwind CSS\n  58 - **State management:** Zustand (client store) + TanStack Query (server state)\n  59 - **Forms:** React Hook Form + Zod validation\n  60 - **i18n:** i18next / react-i18next — supports Arabic (RTL) and English (LTR)\n  61 - **DI container:** tsyringe (decorator-based IoC)\n  62 - **Testing:** Jest + ts-jest + React Testing Library\n  63 \n  64 ---\n  65 \n  66 ## Key Scripts\n  67 \n  68 ```bash\n  69 npm run dev           # Start Next.js dev server (Turbopack, port 9002)\n  70 npm run build         # Production build\n  71 npm run lint          # ESLint\n  72 npm run typecheck     # TypeScript type check (no emit)\n  73 npm run test          # Run Jest tests\n  74 npm run test:watch    # Jest in watch mode\n  75 npm run seed          # Seed local DB (tsx src/lib/db/seed.ts)\n  76 \n  77 # Genkit AI dev server\n  78 npm run genkit:dev    # Start Genkit dev server\n  79 npm run genkit:watch  # Genkit dev server with file watching\n  80 \n  81 # Qdrant vector store\n  82 npm run qdrant:start  # Start Qdrant via Docker Compose\n  83 npm run qdrant:stop   # Stop Qdrant\n  84 npm run qdrant:init   # Initialize Qdrant collections\n  85 npm run qdrant:stats  # Show Qdrant stats\n  86 ```\n  87 \n  88 ---\n  89 \n  90 ## Directory Structure\n  91 \n  92 - `src/app/` — Next.js App Router pages and API routes\n...\n 128 ---\n 129 \n 130 ## Architecture Patterns\n 131 \n 132 ### Clean Architecture (Domain-Driven Design)\n 133 \n...\n 145 ### Dependency Injection\n 146 \n...\n 157 ### AI Flows (Genkit)\n 158 \n...\n 178 ### State Management\n 179 \n...\n 187 ## Coding Conventions\n 188 \n 189 ### TypeScript\n 190 \n...\n 203 ### React / Next.js\n 204 \n...\n 211 ### Styling\n 212 \n...\n 218 ### Components\n 219 \n...\n 225 ### API Routes\n 226 \n...\n 235 ## Firebase & Security\n 236 \n 237 - **Firestore rules** are in `firestore.rules` — always deny by default, whitelist explicitly\n...\n 246 ---\n 247 \n 248 ## RAG System\n 249 \n 250 - Vector store: Qdrant (default collection: `arkan_vectors`, dimension: 768)\n...\n 258 ---\n 259 \n 260 ## Internationalization (i18n)\n 261 \n 262 - Translation keys are in `src/locales/en.json` and `src/locales/ar.json`\n...\n 267 ---\n 268 \n 269 ## Testing\n 270 \n 271 - Test files live alongside source code in `__tests__/` subdirectories\n...\n 279 ---\n 280 \n 281 ## Important Files\n 282 \n 283 | File | Purpose |\n...\n 298 ---\n 299 \n 300 ## Environment Variables (key ones)\n 301 \n 302 ```\n...\n 328 ---\n 329 \n 330 ## Common Pitfalls\n 331 \n 332 - Do not import `firebase-admin` or any server-only module in client components or hooks\n 333 - Do not use `new` to instantiate services — always resolve via `container.resolve()`\n 334 - All Genkit flow files must declare `\'use server\'` at the top\n 335 - **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: AI model names and task constants (`AiModels.ts`) must be located in a dependency-free domain folder. Importing them from server-only SDK entry points (like `Genkit.ts`) pulls heavy Node.js dependencies into the browser bundle, causing Turbopack errors.\n...\n 356 ## Notes\n 357 \n 358 - When converting function-based modules (especially `adapters/api-client/*`) to class-based DI services, treat it as a 3-part refactor: update the module, register it in `src/infrastructure/di/container.ts`, then update every consumer/import in hooks, stores, and components. Skipping the consumer sweep leaves the codebase in a mixed pattern.\n...\n 416 - When working in plan mode, treat the restriction literally: do not use edit/create/delete/bash tools just because the task feels straightforward. Finish readonly exploration, submit the plan, wait for approval, then start implementation in default mode.\n 417 - **`\'use server\'` Export Compliance**: In Next.js 15, files marked with `\'use server\'` can only export **async functions** — not objects (including Genkit Flow objects returned by `ai.defineFlow`). All flow files in `src/modules/ai/infrastructure/flows/` must follow the pattern: 1) `const myFlow = ai.defineFlow(...)` (unexported), 2) `export async function myFlowWrapper(input) { return myFlow(input); }` at the bottom. The existing exported async wrappers are the correct pattern; any `expo